---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import Card from '@components/Card.astro';
import EditorialImage from '@components/EditorialImage.astro';
import ContactPanel from '@components/ContactPanel.astro';
import image from '@assets/images/development-keyboard.webp';
---

<Layout
  title="Web hosting & deployment — Andrew Noblet"
  description="Website deployment, hosting, migration planning, and ongoing care. Explore plans and agree on support, backups, and infrastructure for your project."
>
  <div class="editorial-page">
    <section class="editorial-hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Hosting & deployment</p><h1>
          A home for your site.<br />A plan for its care.
        </h1><p>
          Get your website online and keep the practical details in order. I
          help with deployment, domains, performance, and maintenance so you
          have a clear picture of how your site is run.
        </p><div class="editorial-actions">
          <a class="editorial-button" href="/contact?service=hosting"
            >Discuss your website →</a
          ><a href="/services/hosting/pricing">View hosting plans →</a>
        </div>
      </div><figure><EditorialImage src={image} priority /></figure>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / What I help with</p><h2>
          From the first deployment<br />to ongoing maintenance.
        </h2><p>
          A small static website and an application with a database need
          different infrastructure. We choose the setup and support around your
          actual requirements.
        </p>
      </div><div class="editorial-grid">
        <Card
          ><h3>Website deployment</h3><p>
            Publish a responsive site with custom domains, HTTPS, and a
            repeatable deployment process. Static sites can use a CDN to bring
            files closer to visitors.
          </p><ul>
            <li>Domain and DNS configuration</li><li>
              Git-based builds and deployment
            </li><li>HTTPS and release checks</li>
          </ul></Card
        >
        <Card
          ><h3>Application infrastructure</h3><p>
            Review your runtime, database, and integration needs before choosing
            hosting. Scaling and staging requirements are part of the agreed
            architecture.
          </p><ul>
            <li>Hosting and database planning</li><li>
              Staging and deployment pipelines
            </li><li>Resource and third-party cost review</li>
          </ul></Card
        >
        <Card
          ><h3>Performance & maintenance</h3><p>
            Look at how the site loads and where upkeep is needed. Prioritize
            improvements using measurements and the components your website
            depends on.
          </p><ul>
            <li>Image and caching review</li><li>
              Dependency and security updates
            </li><li>Monitoring and maintenance by agreement</li>
          </ul></Card
        >
        <Card
          ><h3>Migration support</h3><p>
            Plan the move before changing a live service. We review access,
            data, DNS, recovery options, and the possibility of a maintenance
            window.
          </p><ul>
            <li>Existing hosting and data assessment</li><li>
              Transfer and validation plan
            </li><li>Cutover and rollback planning</li>
          </ul></Card
        >
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / How we work</p><h2>
          A deliberate path to launch.
        </h2>
      </div><ol class="process-list">
        <li>
          <h3>Understand</h3><p>
            Review your website, current provider, access, and requirements.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>Agree</h3><p>
            Confirm the environment, costs, backup needs, and support scope.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>Prepare</h3><p>
            Configure the environment and check the deployment or migration
            before cutover.
          </p>
        </li><li>
          <h3>Maintain</h3><p>
            Follow the agreed plan for updates, monitoring, and handling issues.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="editorial-section editorial-split">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Clear expectations</p><h2>
          Know what is covered.
        </h2>
      </div><div class="editorial-prose">
        <p>
          Hosting plans start at $49.99 per month. Your proposal identifies
          provider charges, resources, maintenance responsibilities, and any
          additional services separately.
        </p><p>
          Before work begins, we confirm support hours and response
          expectations, monitoring coverage, backup retention and restoration,
          and any provider uptime terms. Continuous availability and
          zero-downtime migration depend on the setup and are not blanket
          guarantees.
        </p><a href="/services/hosting/pricing">Compare hosting plans →</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <ContactPanel
      title="Let’s talk about your website."
      description="Bring your current URL, hosting provider, and any recurring problems. We’ll identify a practical setup and the care it needs."
      href="/contact?service=hosting"
    />
  </div>
</Layout>
